<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rukun Negara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rukun Negara ('Principles of the Nation') is Malaysia's national philosophy, proclaimed on 31 August 1970 after the racial riots of 13 May 1969 to foster unity among its peoples. Its five principles are belief in God, loyalty to king and country, the supremacy of the constitution, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rule-of-law">rule of law</a>, and courtesy and morality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rukun-negara.jpg" alt="Rukun Negara" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vzach · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TuguNegara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
